#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065206} :activity/id #uuid "4dd7be6e-e9a7-53a7-9076-0bf7c12d09ee" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048919 :topic/id #uuid "cc7fb2dc-62dc-56f4-976f-30935824115a" :topic/math-academy-id 344} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065206 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065396 :tutorial/content "When a function $y=y(x)$ contains complex products, quotients, or radicals, we can use logarithmic differentiation to find the derivative $y'(x)$.\n\nFor example, consider the following function:\n\n$$\ny = x^2 \\cdot 2^x\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find $y'(x)$. To do this, we will use the product rule for logarithms, namely\n\n$$\n\\ln(a b)= \\ln a + \\ln b\n$$\n\nWe differentiate our function by following four steps.\n\n**Step 1.** We take the natural logarithm of both sides and apply the product and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (x^{2}) + \\ln (2^{x}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= 2\\ln x + x\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Next, we differentiate both sides of our equation using implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2\\ln x + x\\ln 2) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2 \\cdot (\\ln x)^{′} + (x)^{′} \\cdot \\ln (2) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + 1 \\cdot \\ln (2) \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= \\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Then, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(\\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4.** Finally, we substitute back our original expression for\n\n$$\ny =x^2\\cdot 2^x{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}(\\frac{2}{x} + \\ln 2) \\\\\n&= x \\cdot 2^{x + 1} + x^{2} \\cdot 2^{x}\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1895a7f3-5ba4-5a31-85b3-6a7b050b307c" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6088 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "caef414d-4f2a-5504-9b92-39a03d2f3c8f" :step/math-academy-id 37035 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065207}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065207 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064309 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064146 :question/id #uuid "c24da7ef-0070-5aae-bade-c82ea56476ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-9845"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7613eee3-a281-57cb-bc47-3b1594920bd1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048773} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050375}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064655} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064662}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product"} :step/id #uuid "b6a516b4-d0c4-5ec7-8f7e-12edd0e85c51" :step/math-academy-id 37036 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065210}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065208 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064310 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064147 :question/id #uuid "7db11c8c-344b-5d87-a8ae-3b006e5bd92b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9846"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71dd9228-4b05-54d9-aeb2-3bdabf89e0e9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049079} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050542}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064653} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064663}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Quotient"} :step/id #uuid "57a60273-bc58-5aff-8dcd-d7139782aa2a" :step/math-academy-id 37037 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065209}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065209 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064311 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064148 :question/id #uuid "e0cec84d-96cf-5fed-ba05-a5cfc57841a1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9847"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6005f9a-3eba-5f8d-909d-894d9cd24d12" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050208} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050496} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050887} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050894}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064652} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064654} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233441}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Radical Expression"} :step/id #uuid "8850f22e-33ee-545a-8f5e-4dc37bda3b30" :step/math-academy-id 37038} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065210 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065397 :tutorial/content "In cases where we wish to differentiate a quotient of functions\n\n$$\ny = f(x) = \\dfrac{g(x)}{h(x)}\n$$\n\nwe can apply the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\ln \\left(\\dfrac{a}{b}\\right) = \\ln a - \\ln b\n$$\n\nFor example, let's compute $y'$, where the function $y$ is given by\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac {e^{x^2}}{(1-2x)^2(x-1)^3}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the natural logarithm of both sides and use the quotient and power rules for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\ln y &= \\ln ((e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})) \\\\\n\\ln y &= \\ln (e^{x^{2}}) - \\ln ((1 - 2x)^{2}) - \\ln ((x - 1)^{3}) \\\\\n\\ln y &= x^{2} - 2\\ln (1 - 2x) - 3\\ln (x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln y) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} - 2\\ln (1 - 2x) - 3\\ln (x - 1)) \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y} \\cdot y^{′} &= 2x - 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - 2x} \\cdot (-2) - 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x - 1} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{′}}{y} &= 2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $y'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= y(2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute our expression for $y$, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^{′} &= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})(2x + \\frac{4}{1 - 2x} - \\frac{3}{x - 1}) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{2}(x - 1)^{3})((2x(1 - 2x)(x - 1) + 4(x - 1) - 3(1 - 2x))/((1 - 2x)(x - 1))) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(2x(1 - 2x)(x - 1) + 4(x - 1) - 3(1 - 2x)) \\\\\n&= (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(-4x^{3} + 6x^{2} + 8x - 7) \\\\\n&= - (e^{x^{2}})/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})(4x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 8x + 7) \\\\\n&= - (e^{x^{2}}(4x^{3} - 6x^{2} - 8x + 7))/((1 - 2x)^{3}(x - 1)^{4})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8cf6e625-669a-5fda-b756-e1ce091eaa93" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6090 :tutorial/title "Using Logarithms to Differentiate a Quotient"} :step/id #uuid "2141558f-a6d2-515d-902a-620581d72401" :step/math-academy-id 37041 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065208}}] :activity/title "Further Logarithmic Differentiation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186064435}]}
